course: dictionary
lesson: 5822
title: A name you can work out
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are names, like Mahabharata, and they can look very hard to read. You can still work out what they mean by reading the words around them. «The Hindu Mahabharata says one should never do to another what one regards as hurtful to oneself.» The word Hindu tells you where it comes from, and says tells you it is a text that teaches something.
explain: The sentence gives you a clue about its meaning. It teaches a rule about how to treat other people kindly, so the Mahabharata is something people read to learn how to live well. You can check this by swapping in your meaning: "The Hindu [a holy book] says one should never do to another what one regards as hurtful to oneself." It still makes sense.
explain: When context is not enough, a dictionary settles it. The Mahabharata is a very long ancient poem from India, and one of the holy books of Hinduism. Now you know what the name means, and you did not need to know it before you started.
fact: The Mahabharata is a very long, ancient poem from India.
fact: It was written in Sanskrit.
fact: It tells the story of a great war between two families of cousins, the Pandavas and the Kauravas.
fact: It is one of the holy books of Hinduism, and it contains the Bhagavad Gita.
fact: Because it is an epic, it is often compared with the Iliad, and it is one of the longest poems ever written.
exercise: «The Hindu Mahabharata says one should never do to another what one regards as hurtful to oneself.» Which religion is the Mahabharata linked to? | Christianity | Judaism | Buddhism | *Hinduism
exercise: What kind of text is the Mahabharata? | A map of India's rivers | A short shopping list | A modern pop song | *A very long ancient poem
exercise: The Mahabharata tells the story of a great war between two families of what? | Farmers | *Cousins | Pirates
test: The Mahabharata was written in which language? | French | Latin | Greek | *Sanskrit
test: In literature, the Mahabharata is called an epic, like which other famous poem? | Hamlet | The Wind in the Willows | The Gruffalo | *The Iliad
exam: Which of these best describes the Mahabharata? | A short cookbook | A type of dance | A map of a city | *A very long ancient poem from India and a holy Hindu text
